### Block 6 - Cascades and orphanRemoval
### Select the "local" environment. Needs data: run the seed in 05-relations.http first.
### Every demo here is rolled back, so you can repeat them as many times as you want.

### Same POST /sales as before, but SaleService no longer saves the items one by one
### (compare git diff jpa-05 jpa-06 -- SaleService.java)
POST {{host}}/sales
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": {{customerId}},
  "items": [
    { "productId": {{productId}}, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### Persist ONLY the sale: how many INSERTs?
### Q: who inserted the items?
POST {{host}}/demo/cascade/persist?customerId={{customerId}}&productId={{productId}}

### orphanRemoval: remove one item from the list -> DELETE
### Q: we never called a repository delete. Who deleted the row?
POST {{host}}/demo/cascade/orphan-removal?saleId={{saleId}}

### Remove the sale: REMOVE cascades to the items
### Q: how is this different from ON DELETE CASCADE in the database?
POST {{host}}/demo/cascade/remove-sale?saleId={{saleId}}

### The trap: CascadeType.REMOVE towards a shared entity (see demo/TrapLine.java)
### Q: what happened to the product when we deleted ONE line?
POST {{host}}/demo/cascade/trap?shared=false

### Same mapping, but another line still references the product: the flush fails
### Q: it only "worked" because of the error. What would happen with a single line?
POST {{host}}/demo/cascade/trap?shared=true
